ACC-021 — Concept Relationship Matrix

Document ID: ACC-021
Title: Concept Relationship Matrix
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the canonical relationships among the Atlas Core Concepts.

The Concept Relationship Matrix establishes how concepts interact, depend upon one another, and participate within the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF). It serves as the authoritative reference for conceptual consistency across all Atlas specifications and implementations.

2. Scope

This specification applies to all canonical concepts defined within Atlas Core Concepts.

It defines:

Concept dependencies
Permitted relationships
Lifecycle participation
Information flow
Cognitive responsibilities

This specification does not define implementation architecture or data models.

3. Canonical Relationship Types

The following relationship types SHALL be used consistently throughout the Atlas ecosystem.

Relationship	Description
Originates From	A concept is created from another concept.
Consumes	A concept uses another concept as input.
Produces	A concept creates another concept as output.
Preserves	A concept retains another concept over time.
Supports	A concept assists another concept.
Governed By	A concept is constrained by a governing concept.
Qualified By	A concept is described by a quality attribute.
Influences	A concept affects another concept without directly producing it.
