7. Normative Requirements

Implementations SHALL:

Preserve all canonical concept relationships.
Avoid introducing circular dependencies unless explicitly defined.
Maintain semantic consistency between concepts.
Preserve traceability across relationships.
Conform to the dependency model defined by this specification.
8. Conformance

A specification conforms to this document if it:

Uses only canonical relationships defined herein.
Does not introduce contradictory dependencies.
Preserves the integrity of the Atlas concept model.
Maintains compatibility with Atlas Core Concepts.
9. Non-Goals

This specification does not:

Define implementation architecture.
Define storage models.
Define APIs.
Define reasoning algorithms.
Define software components.
10. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce additional relationship types, domain-specific concept matrices, semantic mappings, and machine-readable relationship models, provided they remain consistent with the canonical concepts defined by ACC.